Package: sutra
Type: Package
Title: Variance-Preserving Stage-Wise Multi-Environment Trial Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Praveen", family = "Kumar",
                  email = "bkpraveenars@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0000-0000-0000"))
Description: Spatially adjusted genotype means from two-dimensional
    tensor-product P-splines are passed to a stage-wise linear mixed model
    together with their full error variance-covariance matrix, rather than as
    bare point estimates. The second stage whitens that structure by spectral
    decomposition on the genotype-contrast space, so that a standard solver
    reproduces the fully efficient weighted analysis of Piepho and others
    (2012) <doi:10.1002/bimj.201100219>. Unweighted and diagonally weighted
    analyses are provided for direct comparison, a simulation engine with known
    truth is included for validation, and diagnostics report when weighting is
    likely to help or to harm.
